IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 3 (b): ss 26 to 34, deductions from
-- salary, the priority of salary over other debts, and the offence of not paying it.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)" marks the branches that rest on
-- one of the two readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).
--
-- THE MINISTER'S SUBSTITUTES.  Several limits say "one-quarter (or such other proportion
-- prescribed in substitution by the Minister)".  The Minister's substitute is not in the
-- sources, so each such rule takes it as an input that may be NOTHING (no substitute made)
-- and uses the Act's own figure when it is.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 3 Payment of salary, ss 26 to 34`

§§ `s 26 No unauthorised deductions to be made`

-- src:1395 | 26.—(1) No deduction is to be made by an employer from the
-- src:1396 | salary of an employee, unless the deduction is authorised by or under
-- src:1397 | any provision of this Act or is required to be made —
-- src:1399 | (a) by order of a court or other authority competent to make
-- src:1400 | such order;
-- src:1402 | (b) pursuant to a declaration made by the Comptroller of
-- src:1403 | Income Tax under section 57 of the Income Tax Act 1947,
-- src:1404 | the Comptroller of Property Tax under section 38 of the
-- src:1405 | Property Tax Act 1960 or the Comptroller of Goods and
-- src:1410 | Services Tax under section 79 of the Goods and Services
-- src:1411 | Tax Act 1993 that the employer is an agent for recovery of
-- src:1412 | income tax, property tax or goods and services tax (as the
-- src:1413 | case may be) payable by the employee;
-- src:1417 | (c) pursuant to a direction given by the Comptroller of Income
-- src:1418 | Tax under section 91 of the Income Tax Act 1947;
-- src:1424 | (d) pursuant to a declaration made by a MediShield Life
-- src:1425 | Scheme recovery body under section 12 of the MediShield
-- src:1426 | Life Scheme Act 2015 that the employer is an agent for
-- src:1427 | recovery of any outstanding premium (within the meaning
-- src:1428 | of that Act) payable by the employee; or
-- src:1432 | (e) pursuant to a declaration made by a CSHL Scheme
-- src:1433 | recovery body under section 24 of the CareShield Life
-- src:1434 | and Long‑Term Care Act 2019 that the employer is an
-- src:1435 | agent for recovery of any outstanding premium (within the
-- src:1436 | meaning of that Act) payable by the employee.
@ref s 26(1) (src:1395-1436)
GIVEN `the deduction is authorised by or under a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction is required by order of a court or other authority competent to make such order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction is required pursuant to a declaration of the Comptroller of Income Tax, the Comptroller of Property Tax or the Comptroller of Goods and Services Tax that the employer is an agent for recovery of income tax, property tax or goods and services tax payable by the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction is required pursuant to a direction of the Comptroller of Income Tax under section 91 of the Income Tax Act 1947` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction is required pursuant to a declaration of a MediShield Life Scheme recovery body that the employer is an agent for recovery of an outstanding premium payable by the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction is required pursuant to a declaration of a CSHL Scheme recovery body that the employer is an agent for recovery of an outstanding premium payable by the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the employer may make the deduction from the salary of the employee` MEANS
    IF `the deduction is authorised by or under a provision of this Act` OR `the deduction is required by order of a court or other authority competent to make such order` OR `the deduction is required pursuant to a declaration of the Comptroller of Income Tax, the Comptroller of Property Tax or the Comptroller of Goods and Services Tax that the employer is an agent for recovery of income tax, property tax or goods and services tax payable by the employee` OR `the deduction is required pursuant to a direction of the Comptroller of Income Tax under section 91 of the Income Tax Act 1947` OR `the deduction is required pursuant to a declaration of a MediShield Life Scheme recovery body that the employer is an agent for recovery of an outstanding premium payable by the employee` OR `the deduction is required pursuant to a declaration of a CSHL Scheme recovery body that the employer is an agent for recovery of an outstanding premium payable by the employee`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "No deduction is to be made ... unless" says when a deduction is not to be made and does not itself say the deduction is allowed
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No deduction is to be made by an employer from the salary of an employee, unless the deduction is authorised by or under any provision of this Act" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The prohibition of subsection (1), derived from the flat negative (ruling N2): the employer
-- is the bearer, and making the deduction is the breach.
DECLARE `s 26(1) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 26(1) the employer`

DECLARE `s 26(1) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 26(1) make a deduction from the salary of the employee without authority`

@ref s 26(1) (src:1395-1397)
GIVEN `the deduction is authorised or required under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 26(1) Actor` `s 26(1) Action`
`s 26(1) the employer's prohibition on an unauthorised deduction` MEANS
    IF NOT `the deduction is authorised or required under subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY `s 26(1) the employer`
         SHANT `s 26(1) make a deduction from the salary of the employee without authority`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 26(1) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer made a deduction from the salary of the employee that is not authorised by or under this Act and not required under section 26(1)(a) to (e)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1442 | “CSHL Scheme recovery body” has the meaning given by the
-- src:1443 | definition of “recovery body” in section 2(1) of the
-- src:1444 | CareShield Life and Long‑Term Care Act 2019;
@ref s 26(2) "CSHL Scheme recovery body" (src:1442-1444)
GIVEN `the CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019 section 2(1) says the body is a recovery body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) "CSHL Scheme recovery body" the body is one` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by the definition of “recovery body” in section 2(1) of the CareShield Life and Long‑Term Care Act 2019", which is not among the sources
    `the CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019 section 2(1) says the body is a recovery body`

-- src:1446 | “MediShield Life Scheme recovery body” has the meaning
-- src:1447 | given by the definition of “recovery body” in section 2(1) of
-- src:1448 | the MediShield Life Scheme Act 2015.
@ref s 26(2) "MediShield Life Scheme recovery body" (src:1446-1448)
GIVEN `the MediShield Life Scheme Act 2015 section 2(1) says the body is a recovery body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) "MediShield Life Scheme recovery body" the body is one` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by the definition of “recovery body” in section 2(1) of the MediShield Life Scheme Act 2015", which is not among the sources
    `the MediShield Life Scheme Act 2015 section 2(1) says the body is a recovery body`

§§ `s 27 Authorised deductions`

DECLARE `s 27(1) Kind of deduction` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(1)(a) a deduction for absence from work`
    `s 27(1)(b) a deduction for damage to or loss of goods expressly entrusted to the employee for custody, or for loss of money for which the employee is required to account`
    `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer`
    `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer`
    `s 27(1)(f) a deduction for the recovery of an advance, loan or unearned employment benefit, or for the adjustment of an overpayment of salary`
    `s 27(1)(h) a deduction of contributions payable by the employer on behalf of the employee under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`
    `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent`
    `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society`
    `s 27(1)(k) a deduction prescribed`
    `s 27(1) a deduction of some other kind`

-- src:1454 | 27.—(1) The following deductions may be made from the salary of
-- src:1455 | an employee:
-- src:1457 | (a) deductions for absence from work;
-- src:1459 | (b) deductions for damage to or loss of goods expressly
-- src:1460 | entrusted to an employee for custody or for loss of money
-- src:1465 | for which an employee is required to account, where the
-- src:1466 | damage or loss is directly attributable to the employee’s
-- src:1467 | neglect or default;
-- src:1469 | (c) [Deleted by Act 55 of 2018]
-- src:1471 | (d) deductions made with the employee’s written consent for
-- src:1472 | house accommodation supplied by the employer;
-- src:1474 | (e) deductions made with the employee’s written consent for
-- src:1475 | such amenities and services supplied by the employer as
-- src:1476 | the Commissioner may authorise;
-- src:1478 | (f) any deduction for the recovery of any advance, loan or
-- src:1479 | unearned employment benefit, or for the adjustment of any
-- src:1480 | overpayment of salary;
-- src:1482 | (g) [Deleted by Act 26 of 2013]
-- src:1484 | (h) deductions of contributions payable by an employer on
-- src:1485 | behalf of an employee under and in accordance with the
-- src:1486 | provisions of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953;
-- src:1488 | (i) any deduction (other than a deduction mentioned in
-- src:1489 | paragraphs (a) to (h), (j) and (k)) made with the
-- src:1490 | employee’s written consent;
-- src:1492 | (j) deductions made with the employee’s written consent and
-- src:1493 | paid by the employer to any cooperative society registered
-- src:1494 | under any written law for the time being in force in respect
-- src:1495 | of subscriptions, entrance fees, instalments of loans,
-- src:1496 | interest and other dues payable by the employee to such
-- src:1497 | society;
-- src:1499 | (k) any other prescribed deductions.
@ref s 27(1) (src:1454-1499)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 27(1) Kind of deduction`
      `the employee's written consent subsists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damage or loss is directly attributable to the employee's neglect or default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has authorised the amenity or service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributions are payable under and in accordance with the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum is paid to a cooperative society registered under a written law in respect of subscriptions, entrance fees, instalments of loans, interest or other dues payable by the employee to the society` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 27(1)(a) a deduction for absence from work` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 27(1)(b) a deduction for damage to or loss of goods expressly entrusted to the employee for custody, or for loss of money for which the employee is required to account` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the damage or loss is directly attributable to the employee’s neglect or default" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" not met
        IF `the damage or loss is directly attributable to the employee's neglect or default` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deductions made with the employee’s written consent for house accommodation supplied by the employer"
        IF `the employee's written consent subsists` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deductions made with the employee’s written consent for such amenities and services supplied by the employer as the Commissioner may authorise"
        IF `the employee's written consent subsists` AND `the Commissioner has authorised the amenity or service` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `s 27(1)(f) a deduction for the recovery of an advance, loan or unearned employment benefit, or for the adjustment of an overpayment of salary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 27(1)(h) a deduction of contributions payable by the employer on behalf of the employee under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under and in accordance with the provisions of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953"
        IF `the contributions are payable under and in accordance with the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made with the employee’s written consent"
        IF `the employee's written consent subsists` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deductions made with the employee’s written consent and paid by the employer to any cooperative society"
        IF `the employee's written consent subsists` AND `the sum is paid to a cooperative society registered under a written law in respect of subscriptions, entrance fees, instalments of loans, interest or other dues payable by the employee to the society` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `s 27(1)(k) a deduction prescribed` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any other prescribed deductions" are in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the deduction is prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (1) lists deductions that "may be made" and does not say that no other is authorised; section 26(1) says no other is, unless authorised elsewhere in the Act
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1503 | (1A) An employee’s written consent for any deduction mentioned
-- src:1504 | in subsection (1)(d), (e), (i) or (j) may be withdrawn by the employee
-- src:1505 | giving written notice of the withdrawal to the employer at any time
-- src:1506 | before the deduction is made.
@ref s 27(1A) (src:1503-1506)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 27(1) Kind of deduction`
      `the employee gave written consent to the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee gave the employer written notice of the withdrawal before the deduction was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` MEANS
    IF (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer`) OR (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer`) OR (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent`) OR (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society`)
    THEN JUST (`the employee gave written consent to the deduction` AND (NOT `the employee gave the employer written notice of the withdrawal before the deduction was made`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any deduction mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (e), (i) or (j)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1513 | (1B) An employee cannot be penalised for withdrawing a written
-- src:1514 | consent for any deduction mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (e), (i)
-- src:1515 | or (j).
@ref s 27(1B) (src:1513-1515)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 27(1) Kind of deduction`
      `the employee withdrew written consent to the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1B) the employee can be penalised for withdrawing the written consent` MEANS
    IF `the employee withdrew written consent to the deduction` AND ((kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer`) OR (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer`) OR (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent`) OR (kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employee cannot be penalised for withdrawing a written consent for any deduction mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (e), (i) or (j)" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any deduction mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (e), (i) or (j)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1519 | (2) In subsection (1)(e), “services” does not include the supply of
-- src:1520 | tools and raw materials required for the purposes of employment.
@ref s 27(2) (src:1519-1520)
GIVEN `the supply is of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the supply is a service for the purposes of subsection (1)(e)` MEANS
    IF `the supply is of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of employment`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“services” does not include the supply of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of employment"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only what "services" does not include
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1522 | (3) In subsection (1)(f), “employment benefit” —
-- src:1524 | (a) means any benefit that an employee derives from being
-- src:1525 | employed, other than salary; and
-- src:1527 | (b) includes (but is not limited to) benefits such as the
-- src:1528 | following:
-- src:1530 | (i) any annual leave in excess of the annual leave to
-- src:1531 | which the employee is entitled under section 88A;
-- src:1533 | (ii) any flexible employment benefit (such as an
-- src:1534 | allowance that can be utilised, at the employee’s
-- src:1535 | discretion, for any of certain purposes specified in
-- src:1536 | the employee’s contract of service).
@ref s 27(3) (src:1522-1536)
GIVEN `the thing is a benefit that the employee derives from being employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is salary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a flexible employment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than salary" -- the "includes" of paragraph (b) cannot bring salary back in
        IF `the thing is salary` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the thing is annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` OR `the thing is a flexible employment benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the thing is a benefit that the employee derives from being employed` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes (but is not limited to)" benefits such as annual leave beyond section 88A and flexible benefits, so the text does not close the class (marginal (b))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The days of annual leave beyond the entitlement of section 88A.  The entitlement is the
-- answer of section 88A (ea2), taken as an input (seam S4) and passed on when it is NOTHING.
@ref s 27(3)(b)(i) (src:1530-1531)
GIVEN `the days of annual leave the employer gives` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of s 88A the days of paid annual leave` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 27(3)(b)(i) the days of annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 88A the days of paid annual leave`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the entitlement is the answer of section 88A, which may be none
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entitled THEN JUST (IF `the days of annual leave the employer gives` GREATER THAN entitled THEN `the days of annual leave the employer gives` MINUS entitled ELSE 0)

§§ `s 28 Deductions for absence`

-- src:1542 | 28.—(1) Deductions may be made under section 27(1)(a) only on
-- src:1543 | account of the absence of an employee from the place where, by the
-- src:1544 | terms of his or her employment, he or she is required to work, the
-- src:1545 | absence being for the whole or any part of the period during which he
-- src:1546 | or she is so required to work.
@ref s 28(1) (src:1542-1546)
GIVEN `the absence is from the place where, by the terms of the employee's employment, the employee is required to work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is for the whole or any part of the period during which the employee is so required to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) a deduction under section 27(1)(a) may be made on account of the absence` MEANS
    IF `the absence is from the place where, by the terms of the employee's employment, the employee is required to work` AND `the absence is for the whole or any part of the period during which the employee is so required to work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Deductions may be made under section 27(1)(a) only on account of the absence of an employee from the place where" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The largest deduction.  A monthly-rated employee loses the gross rate of pay for one day's
-- work for each day (the Third Schedule's answer, seam S6, may be NOTHING).  For any other
-- employee the deduction may not bear a larger proportion to the salary payable at the gross
-- rate for the salary period than the absence bears to the total period the employee was
-- required to work in it.
-- src:1548 | (2) The amount of any deduction referred to in subsection (1) must
-- src:1549 | not bear a larger proportion to the salary payable at the gross rate of
-- src:1550 | pay to the employee in respect of the salary period for which the
-- src:1551 | deduction is made than the proportion the period for which the
-- src:1552 | employee was absent bears to the total period within such salary
-- src:1553 | period during which the employee was required to work by the terms
-- src:1554 | of his or her employment; and in the case of a monthly‑rated
-- src:1555 | employee the amount of deduction in respect of any one day is the
-- src:1556 | gross rate of pay for one day’s work.
@ref s 28(2) (src:1548-1556)
GIVEN `the employee is monthly-rated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of absence` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the salary payable at the gross rate of pay for the salary period` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the absence` IS A NUMBER
      `the total period during which the employee was required to work in the salary period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 28(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the employee is monthly-rated` THEN
            CONSIDER `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the gross rate of pay for one day’s work" is the Third Schedule's answer, which may be none
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (rate TIMES `the days of absence`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the total period required to work is nothing, and the proportion has no meaning
        IF `the total period during which the employee was required to work in the salary period` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the salary payable at the gross rate of pay for the salary period` TIMES (`the length of the absence` DIVIDED BY `the total period during which the employee was required to work in the salary period`))

-- src:1561 | (3) If any employee absents himself or herself from work otherwise
-- src:1562 | than as provided by this Act or by his or her contract of service, the
-- src:1563 | employer may, subject to any order which may be made by a court or
-- src:1564 | by the Commissioner on complaint of either party, deduct from any
-- src:1565 | salary due to the employee the cost of food supplied to him or her
-- src:1566 | during his or her absence.
@ref s 28(3) (src:1561-1566)
GIVEN `the employee absents himself or herself from work otherwise than as provided by this Act or by the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court or the Commissioner on complaint of either party has made an order to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) the employer may deduct from salary due the cost of food supplied during the absence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any employee absents himself or herself from work otherwise than as provided by this Act or by his or her contract of service" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if"
        IF NOT `the employee absents himself or herself from work otherwise than as provided by this Act or by the contract of service` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `a court or the Commissioner on complaint of either party has made an order to the contrary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any order which may be made by a court or by the Commissioner on complaint of either party" -- the order is not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 29 Deductions for damages or loss`

-- The largest deduction under section 27(1)(b): not more than the loss, and, unless the
-- Commissioner permits, not more than one-quarter (or the Minister's substitute) of one
-- month's wages.
-- src:1570 | 29.—(1) A deduction under section 27(1)(b) must not exceed the
-- src:1571 | amount of the damages or loss caused to the employer by the neglect
-- src:1572 | or default of the employee and, except with the Commissioner’s
-- src:1573 | permission, must not in any case exceed one‑quarter (or such other
-- src:1574 | proportion prescribed in substitution by the Minister) of one month’s
-- src:1575 | wages and must not be made until the employee has been given an
-- src:1576 | opportunity of showing cause against the deduction.
@ref s 29(1) (src:1570-1576)
GIVEN `the damages or loss caused to the employer by the neglect or default of the employee` IS A NUMBER
      `one month's wages` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction`
    THEN `the damages or loss caused to the employer by the neglect or default of the employee`
    ELSE min `the damages or loss caused to the employer by the neglect or default of the employee` (`one month's wages` TIMES proportion)
    WHERE
        proportion MEANS
            CONSIDER `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.25
            WHEN JUST p THEN p

@ref s 29(1) (src:1570-1576)
GIVEN `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) the deduction under section 27(1)(b) may be made now` MEANS
    IF `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says the deduction "must not be made until" the opportunity has been given, and does not say that it may be made after
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made until the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE
-- The same "until" as a bar of its own (ruled 2026-11-05, the until-bar rule): JUST TRUE
-- before the opportunity has been given, JUST FALSE once it has.  The question above
-- ("may it be made now") is never answered yes on the strength of the bar alone.
@ref s 29(1) (src:1570-1576)
GIVEN `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) the bar on making the deduction under section 27(1)(b) applies` MEANS
    IF `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made until the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction" -- the bar is lifted once the opportunity has been given
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1580 | (2) All such deductions and all realisations thereof must be
-- src:1581 | recorded in a register to be kept by the employer in such form as
-- src:1582 | may be prescribed.
@ref s 29(2) (src:1580-1582)
GIVEN `the deduction or its realisation is recorded in the register kept by the employer in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the employer has recorded the deduction or its realisation in the register` MEANS
    `the deduction or its realisation is recorded in the register kept by the employer in the prescribed form`

§§ `s 30 Deductions for accommodation, amenity and service`

-- The largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e): not more than the value of what was
-- supplied, and, with all other deductions under those two paragraphs in the salary period,
-- not more than one-quarter (or the Minister's substitute) of the salary payable for it.
-- src:1588 | (2) Any deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e) must not exceed an
-- src:1589 | amount equivalent to the value of the house accommodation, amenity
-- src:1590 | or service supplied, and the total amount of all deductions under
-- src:1591 | section 27(1)(d) and (e) made from an employee’s salary by his or her
-- src:1592 | employer in any one salary period must not in any case exceed
-- src:1593 | one‑quarter (or such other proportion prescribed in substitution by the
-- src:1594 | Minister) of the salary payable to the employee in respect of that
-- src:1595 | period.
@ref s 30(2) (src:1588-1595)
GIVEN `the value of the house accommodation, amenity or service supplied` IS A NUMBER
      `the deductions already made under section 27(1)(d) and (e) in the salary period` IS A NUMBER
      `the salary payable for the salary period` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e)` MEANS
    min `the value of the house accommodation, amenity or service supplied` (max 0 ((`the salary payable for the salary period` TIMES proportion) MINUS `the deductions already made under section 27(1)(d) and (e) in the salary period`))
    WHERE
        proportion MEANS
            CONSIDER `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.25
            WHEN JUST p THEN p

-- src:1599 | (3) In the case of a deduction under section 27(1)(e), the deduction
-- src:1600 | is subject to such conditions as the Commissioner may impose.
@ref s 30(3) (src:1599-1600)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 27(1) Kind of deduction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3) the deduction is subject to conditions that the Commissioner may impose` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a deduction under section 27(1)(e)"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 31 Recovery of advances and loans`

-- src:1609 | 31.—(1) The recovery of an advance of money made to an
-- src:1610 | employee before the commencement of a contract of service is to
-- src:1611 | begin from the first payment of salary in respect of a completed salary
-- src:1612 | period, but no recovery may be made of any such advance made for
-- src:1613 | travelling expenses.
@ref s 31(1) (src:1609-1613)
GIVEN `the advance of money was made to the employee before the commencement of the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is the first payment of salary in respect of a completed salary period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the recovery of the advance may begin with the payment` MEANS
    IF `the advance of money was made to the employee before the commencement of the contract of service`
    THEN JUST `the payment is the first payment of salary in respect of a completed salary period`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an advance of money made to an employee before the commencement of a contract of service"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 31(1) (src:1609-1613)
GIVEN `the advance of money was made to the employee before the commencement of the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advance was made for travelling expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the advance may be recovered` MEANS
    IF `the advance of money was made to the employee before the commencement of the contract of service` AND `the advance was made for travelling expenses`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no recovery may be made of any such advance made for travelling expenses" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) says when recovery of an advance begins and does not say it may be recovered; subsections (2) and (3) do
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1615 | (2) Advances may be recovered in instalments by deductions from
-- src:1616 | salary spread over not more than 12 months.
@ref s 31(2) (src:1615-1616)
GIVEN `the number of months over which the deductions from salary are spread` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the advance is recovered in instalments within the permitted spread` MEANS
    `the number of months over which the deductions from salary are spread` AT MOST 12

-- src:1618 | (3) An instalment under subsection (2) must not exceed one‑quarter
-- src:1619 | (or such other proportion prescribed in substitution by the Minister)
-- src:1620 | of the salary due for the salary period in respect of which the
-- src:1621 | deduction is made.
@ref s 31(3) (src:1618-1621)
GIVEN `the salary due for the salary period in respect of which the deduction is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 31(3) the largest instalment of an advance` MEANS
    `the salary due for the salary period in respect of which the deduction is made` TIMES proportion
    WHERE
        proportion MEANS
            CONSIDER `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.25
            WHEN JUST p THEN p

-- src:1625 | (4) Loans may be recovered in instalments by deductions from
-- src:1626 | salary.
@ref s 31(4) (src:1625-1626)
GIVEN `the sum is a loan to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) the loan may be recovered in instalments by deductions from salary` MEANS
    IF `the sum is a loan to the employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Loans may be recovered in instalments by deductions from salary"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1628 | (5) An instalment under subsection (4) must not exceed one‑quarter
-- src:1629 | (or such other proportion prescribed in substitution by the Minister)
-- src:1630 | of the salary due for the salary period in respect of which the
-- src:1631 | deduction is made.
@ref s 31(5) (src:1628-1631)
GIVEN `the salary due for the salary period in respect of which the deduction is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 31(5) the largest instalment of a loan` MEANS
    `the salary due for the salary period in respect of which the deduction is made` TIMES proportion
    WHERE
        proportion MEANS
            CONSIDER `the proportion the Minister has prescribed in substitution`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.25
            WHEN JUST p THEN p

§§ `s 32 Deductions not to exceed prescribed limit`

-- The largest total of deductions in a salary period, other than deductions under
-- section 27(1)(a), (f) or (j): 50% (or the Minister's substitute) of the salary payable.
-- src:1637 | 32.—(1) The total amount of all deductions made from an
-- src:1638 | employee’s salary by an employer in any one salary period, other
-- src:1639 | than deductions under section 27(1)(a), (f) or (j), must not exceed
-- src:1640 | 50% (or such other percentage prescribed in substitution by the
-- src:1641 | Minister) of the salary payable to the employee in respect of that
-- src:1642 | period.
@ref s 32(1) (src:1637-1642)
GIVEN `the salary payable to the employee in respect of the salary period` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage the Minister has prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 32(1) the largest total of deductions in the salary period` MEANS
    `the salary payable to the employee in respect of the salary period` TIMES (percentage DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        percentage MEANS
            CONSIDER `the percentage the Minister has prescribed in substitution`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 50
            WHEN JUST p THEN p

@ref s 32(1) (src:1637-1642)
GIVEN `the total of the deductions in the salary period, other than deductions under section 27(1)(a), (f) or (j)` IS A NUMBER
      `the salary payable to the employee in respect of the salary period` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage the Minister has prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) the total of the deductions is within the limit` MEANS
    `the total of the deductions in the salary period, other than deductions under section 27(1)(a), (f) or (j)` AT MOST `s 32(1) the largest total of deductions in the salary period` `the salary payable to the employee in respect of the salary period` `the percentage the Minister has prescribed in substitution`

-- src:1646 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to deductions made from the last
-- src:1647 | salary due to an employee on termination of his or her contract of
-- src:1648 | service or on completion of his or her contract of service.
@ref s 32(2) (src:1646-1648)
GIVEN `the deduction is made from the last salary due on termination or on completion of the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) subsection (1) applies to the deduction` MEANS
    IF `the deduction is made from the last salary due on termination or on completion of the contract of service`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to deductions made from the last salary due to an employee on termination of his or her contract of service or on completion of his or her contract of service" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only when subsection (1) does not apply
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 33 Priority of salary to other debts`

-- The monthly salary measured against the ceiling: "excluding overtime payments, bonus
-- payments, annual wage supplements, productivity incentive payments and any allowance however
-- described".  The keel's salary already leaves out a travelling allowance (s 2(1) "salary"),
-- so only the other allowances are taken off here.  The amounts must be for a month.
-- src:1655 | 33.—(1) This section applies —
-- src:1657 | (a) to workmen who are in receipt of a salary not exceeding
-- src:1658 | $4,500 a month (excluding overtime payments, bonus
-- src:1659 | payments, annual wage supplements, productivity
-- src:1660 | incentive payments and any allowance however
-- src:1661 | described) or such other amount as the Minister may
-- src:1662 | prescribe; and
-- src:1664 | (b) to every employee (other than a workman or a person
-- src:1665 | employed in a managerial or an executive position) who
-- src:1666 | receives a salary not exceeding $2,600 a month (excluding
-- src:1667 | any overtime payment, bonus payment, annual wage
-- src:1668 | supplement, productivity incentive payment and any
-- src:1669 | allowance however described) or such other amount as
-- src:1670 | the Minister may prescribe.
@ref s 33(1) (src:1655-1670)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 33(1) the monthly salary measured against the ceiling` MEANS
    IF pay's `the amounts are for` EQUALS `Pay is fixed for each month`
    THEN JUST (`s 2(1) "salary" the amount` pay MINUS sum (LIST pay's `overtime payments`, pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`, pay's `productivity incentive payments`, pay's `food allowances`, pay's `housing allowances`, pay's `allowances of any other kind`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the ceilings are stated "a month" and the text does not say how to restate another basis of pay as a month
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1657 | (a) to workmen who are in receipt of a salary not exceeding
-- src:1658 | $4,500 a month (excluding overtime payments, bonus
-- src:1659 | payments, annual wage supplements, productivity
-- src:1660 | incentive payments and any allowance however
-- src:1661 | described) or such other amount as the Minister may
-- src:1662 | prescribe; and
@ref s 33(1)(a) (src:1657-1662)
GIVEN `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the monthly salary measured against the ceiling` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount the Minister has prescribed in substitution for $4,500` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1)(a) the person is a workman to whom this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "workmen who are in receipt of a salary not exceeding $4,500 a month" -- a person who is not a workman is outside paragraph (a) (marginal (a))
        IF NOT `the person is a workman` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the monthly salary measured against the ceiling`
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the salary measured against the ceiling is not known
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST salary THEN JUST (salary AT MOST ceiling)
    WHERE
        ceiling MEANS
            CONSIDER `the amount the Minister has prescribed in substitution for $4,500`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 4500
            WHEN JUST c THEN c

-- src:1664 | (b) to every employee (other than a workman or a person
-- src:1665 | employed in a managerial or an executive position) who
-- src:1666 | receives a salary not exceeding $2,600 a month (excluding
-- src:1667 | any overtime payment, bonus payment, annual wage
-- src:1668 | supplement, productivity incentive payment and any
-- src:1669 | allowance however described) or such other amount as
-- src:1670 | the Minister may prescribe.
@ref s 33(1)(b) (src:1664-1670)
GIVEN `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the monthly salary measured against the ceiling` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount the Minister has prescribed in substitution for $2,600` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1)(b) the employee is one to whom this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every employee (other than a workman or a person employed in a managerial or an executive position)" -- marginal (a)
        IF `the person is a workman` OR `the person is employed in a managerial or an executive position` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the monthly salary measured against the ceiling`
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the salary measured against the ceiling is not known
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST salary THEN JUST (salary AT MOST ceiling)
    WHERE
        ceiling MEANS
            CONSIDER `the amount the Minister has prescribed in substitution for $2,600`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 2600
            WHEN JUST c THEN c

-- Subsection (3) says what the subsection (2) rule reaches: these four kinds of property and
-- money only.
DECLARE `s 33(3) Kind of property or money` IS ONE OF
    `s 33(3)(a) property on which the employees were or are working`
    `s 33(3)(b) property that was or is the produce of the work of the employees`
    `s 33(3)(c) movable property used or being used by the employees in the course of their work`
    `s 33(3)(d) money due to the employer in respect of work done by the employees`
    `s 33(3) property or money of some other kind`

-- src:1684 | (3) This section applies only —
-- src:1686 | (a) to property on which those employees were or are working;
-- src:1688 | (b) where the property sold was or is the produce of the work
-- src:1689 | of those employees;
-- src:1691 | (c) where the property sold is movable property used or being
-- src:1692 | used by those employees in the course of their work; or
-- src:1694 | (d) to money due to the employer in respect of work done by
-- src:1695 | those employees.
@ref s 33(3) (src:1684-1695)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 33(3) Kind of property or money`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(3) subsection (2) applies to the property or money` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 33(3) property or money of some other kind` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only —" -- marginal (a)
        JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (2): the court must not distribute the proceeds until it has ascertained and paid
-- the salary due.  The provision addresses only the court, so layer 1 holds it as the answer to
-- "may the proceeds be distributed" and the seat does not ask it.
-- src:1674 | (2) When, on the application of a person holding a mortgage,
-- src:1675 | charge or lien or of a person who has obtained a judgment or decree,
-- src:1676 | the property of an employer is sold, or any money due to the employer
-- src:1677 | is garnished, the court ordering the sale or garnishment must not
-- src:1678 | distribute the proceeds of the sale or the money to the person entitled
-- src:1679 | thereto unless the court has ascertained and paid the salary due to all
-- src:1680 | the employees employed by that employer and to all employees
-- src:1681 | engaged by a contractor or subcontractor and working for that
-- src:1682 | employer.
@ref s 33(2) (src:1674-1682)
GIVEN `the property of an employer is sold, or money due to the employer is garnished, on the application of a person holding a mortgage, charge or lien or of a person who has obtained a judgment or decree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ascertained and paid the salary due to all the employees employed by that employer and to all employees engaged by a contractor or subcontractor and working for that employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the court may distribute the proceeds or the money to the person entitled` MEANS
    IF `the property of an employer is sold, or money due to the employer is garnished, on the application of a person holding a mortgage, charge or lien or of a person who has obtained a judgment or decree` AND (NOT `the court has ascertained and paid the salary due to all the employees employed by that employer and to all employees engaged by a contractor or subcontractor and working for that employer`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court ordering the sale or garnishment must not distribute the proceeds of the sale or the money to the person entitled thereto unless the court has ascertained and paid the salary due" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must not distribute ... unless" says when the court must not distribute and does not say the court may
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1700 | (4) The amount payable to each such employee under
-- src:1701 | subsection (2) must not exceed 5 months’ salary.
@ref s 33(4) (src:1700-1701)
GIVEN `the salary due to the employee` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's monthly salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 33(4) the most payable to the employee under subsection (2)` MEANS
    min `the salary due to the employee` (5 TIMES `the employee's monthly salary`)

-- src:1707 | (7) In this section, “employees” is deemed to include
-- src:1708 | subcontractors for labour and “salary” is deemed to include money
-- src:1709 | due to a subcontractor for labour.
@ref s 33(7) (src:1707-1709)
GIVEN `the person is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subcontractor for labour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(7) the person is an employee for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person is an employee` OR `the person is a subcontractor for labour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“employees” is deemed to include subcontractors for labour", which opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 33(7) (src:1707-1709)
GIVEN `the sum is money due to a subcontractor for labour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum is salary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(7) the sum is salary for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the sum is salary` OR `the sum is money due to a subcontractor for labour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“salary” is deemed to include money due to a subcontractor for labour", which opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 34 Offence`

-- src:1713 | 34.—(1) Any employer who fails to pay salary in accordance with
-- src:1714 | the provisions of this Part shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 34(1) (src:1713-1714)
GIVEN `the employer fails to pay salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer fails to pay salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any employer who fails to pay salary in accordance with the provisions of this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The form seam S14 asks for: the offence "under section 21, 22 or 23".
@ref s 34(1) (src:1713-1714)
GIVEN `the employer contravenes section 21, 22 or 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34 the employer is guilty of an offence under s 21, 22 or 23` MEANS
    IF `the employer contravenes section 21, 22 or 23`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any employer who fails to pay salary in accordance with the provisions of this Part", read with subsection (2): "for contravening section 21, 22 or 23"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (1) states no penalty of its own for the other sections of the Part.  The
-- penalty "for which no penalty is otherwise provided" is in section 112 (ea2), which the
-- caller's answer carries (seam S15; SEAMS-FOUND.md).
@ref s 34(1) (src:1713-1714)
GIVEN `the answer of s 112 first conviction` IS A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
      `the answer of s 112 subsequent conviction` IS A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
      `the employer has been convicted of an offence before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 34(1) the penalty on conviction where the failure is not a contravention of section 21, 22 or 23` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (1) states no penalty, and the penalty for which none is otherwise provided is in section 112
    IF `the employer has been convicted of an offence before` THEN `the answer of s 112 subsequent conviction` ELSE `the answer of s 112 first conviction`

-- src:1731 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), a person is a repeat offender
-- src:1732 | in relation to an offence under subsection (1) if the person who is
-- src:1733 | convicted or found guilty of an offence under subsection (1) of
-- src:1734 | contravening section 21, 22 or 23 (called the current offence) has
-- src:1735 | been convicted or found guilty of an offence of contravening
-- src:1736 | section 21, 22 or 23 on at least one other occasion (whether before, on
-- src:1737 | or after 1 April 2014) before the date on which the person is convicted
-- src:1738 | or found guilty of the current offence.
@ref s 34(3) (src:1731-1738)
GIVEN `the date on which the person is convicted or found guilty of the current offence` IS A DATE
      `the dates on which the person was convicted or found guilty of an offence of contravening section 21, 22 or 23 on other occasions` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` MEANS
    -- the text counts occasions "whether before, on or after 1 April 2014", so no earlier limit is put on them
    any (GIVEN d YIELD d LESS THAN `the date on which the person is convicted or found guilty of the current offence`) `the dates on which the person was convicted or found guilty of an offence of contravening section 21, 22 or 23 on other occasions`

-- src:1718 | (2) Any employer who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:1719 | for contravening section 21, 22 or 23 shall be liable on conviction —
-- src:1721 | (a) to a fine of not less than $3,000 and not more than $15,000
-- src:1722 | or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:1723 | both; and
-- src:1725 | (b) if the employer is a repeat offender, to a fine of not less
-- src:1726 | than $6,000 and not more than $30,000 or to imprisonment
-- src:1727 | for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 34(2) (src:1718-1727)
GIVEN `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) for contravening section 21, 22 or 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 34(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any employer who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) for contravening section 21, 22 or 23 shall be liable on conviction"
        IF NOT `the employer is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) for contravening section 21, 22 or 23` THEN NOTHING
        -- (b) governs a repeat offender: the higher range (fork F-34(2), NOTES.md)
        IF `the employer is a repeat offender` THEN JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 6000, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 30000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 3000, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 15000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6)
